  "worked_solution": "The distance between $f(t)=8t-3$ and $g(t)=2t-1$ with respect to the given inner product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\u2016f(t)-g(t)\u2016 \\\\  & =\u20168t-3-(2t-1)\u2016 \\\\  & =\u20166t-2\u2016 \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\u27e86t-2,6t-2\u27e9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u27e86t-2,6t-2\u27e9 & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(6t-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(36{t}^{2}-24t+4)\\text{d}t \\\\  & =[12{t}^{3}-12{t}^{2}+4t]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(12-12+4)-0 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the distance is $d=\\sqrt{4}=2.$",
